    "body": "@domenic I think the second option is closer to what browsers do today. [Gecko uses `any`](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/dom/webidl/Console.webidl#37). This doesn't throw in Safari/Chrome/Firefox:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nlet o = {}; Object.defineProperty(o, \"x\", { get() { throw \"y\" } }); console.table(o);\r\n```",
